      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum daily dose, and I can't think of an indication that justifies it. The extra dose adds risk without adding benefit, because ibuprofen's analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects plateau well below this. You're the attending and the decision is yours. But I don't want to put an order into the system that I expect to cause serious harm, and you haven't given a clinical rationale.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** For example, 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the ceiling). Tell me which one and I'll enter it now.\n- **Enter 400 mg PO four times daily** if 1,600 mg/day was what you meant.\n- **Discuss the case with pharmacy.** If you think this patient has an unusual need, a pharmacist can review it with you. Any order that exceeds the maximum should go through their review and your institution's override process, not be entered directly through me.\n\nIf you'd like a different option, such as adding acetaminophen or another agent for more analgesia, I can enter that too."
      }
